          "text": "The pattern is consistent with a **monoclinically distorted, cation-ordered rutile derivative**. The indexed metric is approximately \\(a \\simeq c \\simeq 4.552\\) \u00c5, \\(b \\simeq 3.333\\) \u00c5, and \\(\\beta \\simeq 94.2^\\circ\\), with \\(Z=1\\). Li and V occupy the two alternating octahedral cation sites. The conservative structural assignment is **P2/m (No. 10)**; lowering it to \\(P\\overline1\\) does not produce a distinct topology.\n\nRepresentative indexing includes 19.53\u00b0 from the nearly coincident 100/001 family, 26.72\u00b0 from 010, 33.31\u00b0 from 110/011, 55.04\u00b0 from 020, 85.48\u00b0 from 400/004, and 87.75\u00b0 from 030. Several other features are unresolved monoclinic multiplets.\n\n```cif\ndata_LiVF4_ordered_rutile\n_audit_creation_method              'Powder-pattern indexing and ordered-rutile model'\n_chemical_name_common               'lithium vanadium(III) fluoride'\n_chemical_formula_structural        'LiVF4'\n_chemical_formula_sum               'Li V F4'\n_cell_formula_units_Z               1\n\n_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M       'P 1 2/m 1'\n_symmetry_Int_Tables_number          10\n_space_group_crystal_system          monoclinic\n\n_cell_length_a                       4.5520\n_cell_length_b                       3.3330\n_cell_length_c                       4.5520\n_cell_angle_alpha                    90\n_cell_angle_beta                     94.20\n_cell_angle_gamma                    90\n_cell_volume                         68.84\n\n_diffrn_radiation_type               'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength         1.5406\n\nloop_\n_space_group_symop_id\n_space_group_symop_operation_xyz\n1 'x,y,z'\n2 '-x,y,-z'\n3 '-x,-y,-z'\n4 'x,-y,z'\n\nloop_\n_atom_type_symbol\n_atom_type_oxidation_number\nLi  1\nV   3\nF  -1\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_U_iso_or_equiv\nLi1 Li 1 0.0000 0.0000 0.0000 1.0 0.012\nV1  V  1 0.5000 0.5000 0.5000 1.0 0.008\nF1  F  2 0.3230 0.0000 0.3230 1.0 0.012\nF2  F  2 0.7950 0.5000 0.2050 1.0 0.012\n```\n\nThe fluorine coordinates are chemically constrained starting values rather than uniquely refined values; they give Li\u2013F distances of approximately 2.00\u20132.04 \u00c5 and V\u2013F distances of approximately 1.97\u20132.00 \u00c5.",
